when you look at the Mount Charleston  Lodge not only includes the possibility  of a new restaurant but maybe even a new  hotel you might recall the Lodge at the  end of Kyle Canyon Road was destroyed by  fire September of 2021. and Mary Jane  bellies shares how residents are  reacting and what this could mean for  their town  it's been more than a year since the  Mount Charleston Lodge burned down it  was a home away from home for Valley  locals and hikers so in the announcement  of a new Lodge was in the works we're  all excited for a new Lodge to be built  fill fill a hole that was  that that happened when the the lodge  burnt down many residents eager to see  what would become of the Historic Site  resident Boca attended the Mount  Charleston Town Advisory board meeting  on December 1st Boca says there is some  pushback from Old Town residents about  the possibility of a new hotel going up  at the lodge the only concerns I think a  lot of us have are they want to put a  hotel in which would bring a lot of  traffic and  you know we have water issues and  ecological impacts that might come from  that they said maybe it'd be about 30 to  34 rooms  um and we had a meeting down at the  library at a community meeting and they  wanted to get some feedback  um and a bunch of us in the community  are very opposed to the hotel but very  excited about a rebuilding of the lodge  nationally Ryan agrees with Boca she  moved to Mount Charleston two years ago  so I think that there are some concerns  from the residents just for many reasons  light pollution being one of them  um just extra traffic on a already  notoriously dangerous road I think  especially during the winter time there  are a lot of animals and I think that a  lot of folks don't know you know not to  walk up to the horses and things like  that while Boca understands the long  development project ahead she hopes  residents concerns will be considered of  course this is residential area and they  don't have the permits for that and it's  likely that they won't get it I know  that there's going to be a big fight  from the residents here if they try to  do that but we're very supportive of a  rebuild of a lodge  8 news now reached out to the owners of  the Mount Charleston Lodge which is  Ellis Island while there are no  interviews about potential plans at this  time we did receive this statement they  say they've been working on it for the  past year but they are still in the  initial stages end quote we shared our  vision including conceptual plans and  renderings we look forward to working  with the community and Clark County to  re-establish the Mount Charleston Lodge
 

